meta {
  name: Make Payment All (Combined)
  type: http
  seq: 42
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/payments-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "totalAmount": 500,
    "paymentMode": "CASH"
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Receive ONE combined payment across a combined order's CHILD sub-orders in a
  single atomic transaction (Registration/Finance → Billings → "Make Payment
  All"). `:id` may be the PARENT order or either CHILD — both resolve to the same
  parent, and the payment is spread across all of its ACTIVE (non-cancelled)
  sub-orders. All amounts are rupees (up to 2 decimal places).

  Supply EXACTLY ONE of:
  - `totalAmount` (≥0.01) — the server auto-distributes it across the sub-orders by
    the **creation ratio** (each sub-order's net share), **capped at each
    sub-order's remaining balance**; any overflow spills to the other sub-order.
    e.g. diagnostic net 1400 / radiology net 600 ⇒ a 500 payment → 350 / 150.
  - `allocations` — an explicit per-sub-order amount (manual override):
    `[{ "orderId": "<child id>", "paidAmount": 350 }, { "orderId": "<child id>", "paidAmount": 150 }]`.
    A 0 amount skips that sub-order.

  Always required:
  - `paymentMode` — `CASH | CREDIT | UPI | CARD | WALLET | BANK_TRANSFER`.
  - `reference?`, `paymentDate?` (ISO), `notes?` — optional, stored on every row.

  Validation (nothing is written if any check fails — the whole transaction rolls
  back):
  - exactly one of `totalAmount` / `allocations`, and a positive total to collect,
    else 422 `COMBINED_PAYMENT_INVALID`.
  - each allocation's `orderId` must be an active CHILD of this parent, else 422
    `SUB_ORDER_NOT_IN_PARENT`.
  - no sub-order may be overpaid beyond its server-computed pending balance, else
    422 `SUB_ORDER_OVERPAYMENT`.
  - `:id` must resolve to a combined order, else 422 `NOT_A_COMBINED_ORDER`
    (404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if missing / other tenant).
  - collection-by-other-user gate (same as `POST /payments`): a non-creator needs
    the branch setting `AllowCollectionOfAmountByOtherUser` ON plus the
    `REG_SETTLE_PAYMENT_OTHERS` permission.

  Writes one PAYMENT `PaymentDetails` row per sub-order that received money (the
  ledger is append-only), recomputes each sub-order's `paymentStatus` / `billStatus`,
  then re-aggregates the PARENT once. Returns the parent's sub-orders, fully
  composed, with their new balances (same shape as `GET /orders/:id/sub-orders`).

  NOTE: `{{orderId}}` must be a COMBINED order's parent or child id. Create one on
  `/registration/create` with both lab and radiology items, then use its id.
}
